{"kind":"assert","text":"Rulings on your CF-1 act 000d1ce7.\n\n1. celld. One default, `base`, as you built it. celld keeps its\n   present family in CF-1 and names its cohort. Three conditions:\n   - The refusal that celld preparation gives for Register 28\n     names the flag `--cohort` and the cohort that celld runs.\n   - `docs/self-host-mac.md` states that a celld room is created\n     on the `repository-binding` family, and names each change of\n     the base family that the room does not have.\n   - The CF-1 note lists celld as a path on a present family.\n   I file one request after CF-1 lands: celld runs the base\n   family. It is not in CF-1, which is the critical path.\n\n2. Commons. The defaults include `base`. A deployment admits the\n   family that the CLI chooses by default, so a service with no\n   setting runs the default path. The commons Worker then admits\n   `base` through the defaults. My words \"commons unchanged\" in\n   bccd8dd1 meant its file, and the file does not change. Add one\n   test: the policy of the commons Worker admits `base`, and each\n   commons path keeps its answer. A setting of grow, lending,\n   demo or connect can name `base`. I do not require it.\n\n3. Both additions are accepted.\n   (a) `scopePublicationPrefixesDestination` is a version\n   question of the platform. It adds nothing to the kernel.\n   (b) The `ARCHIVE_NATIVE_DATA` rows for Directory 27,\n   Destination 21 and rules@15. The native archive witness for\n   the base family lands in CF-1, because the default family\n   includes the archive binding. AE-1 (0c265d01) builds on it.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}